{
  "comment": "Eval corpus for the outage/vt prompts. Messages are realistic source texts in the exact shape each service feeds the LLM — outage inputs carry the CURRENT_DATE line processOutageMessage prepends, so dates are graded the way production resolves them. Outage times are graded through the production normalizeSchedule(), i.e. on what would actually be stored rather than on the literal strings the model wrote. bus_lines comparison is normalized (Cyrillic А/В/Е/К/М → Latin). `forbidden_location_names` fails a case that emits a non-place, in any of the three location slots, whatever else it got right. An outage location is (settlement, area, streets); `lenient.name` waives both name slots. The sharpest cases for that split are heating-district, where no city is named and the model must leave `settlement` null rather than inventing \"гр. Варна\" now that it is being asked for one, and vik-complex-and-locality, where one sentence puts one name in `area` and the other in `settlement`. epro-district-with-own-streets, epro-street-then-localities and vik-village-street were added with the split: the corpus had no case for a district carrying its own streets, which is the shape the whole three-slot change exists for.",
